---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "Rules & Multi-Destination Management";
const pageDesc = "Manage routing tasks with many-to-many fan-out, source aggregation, cloning, priority order and origin masking through an intermediate channel.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Features', href: url('/features/') },
    { name: 'Rules & Destinations', href: url('/features/rules-and-destinations/') },
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'Automated Forwarding', href: url('/features/automated-forwarding/') }}
  next={{ title: 'Text Cleaner', href: url('/features/text-cleaner/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>ForwardRule</strong> is the fundamental unit of routing in AutoTelegramForward. Each rule links one or more source chats to one or more destination targets, binding custom filters, cleaners, and headers/footers to that specific pipeline.
    </p>

    <h2 id="fan-out">1-to-Many Fan-Out Routing</h2>
    <p>
      Publish once, distribute everywhere. A single source update can automatically be delivered to multiple destinations across different accounts or bots simultaneously:
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs my-4 text-slate-300">
      Source: @PrimaryNewsChannel<br />
      ├── Destination A: @EnglishSummaryChannel (Clean Copy + English Footer)<br />
      ├── Destination B: -1001892348271 (VIP Private Group)<br />
      └── Destination C: -1001928374928/42 (Forum Supergroup Topic #42)
    </div>

    <h2 id="rule-duplication">Instant Rule Duplication (rdup)</h2>
    <p>
      Creating complex rules with intricate cleaner flags, headers, and filters for dozens of channels can be time-consuming. AutoTelegramForward provides an instant <strong>Rule Duplicate</strong> feature:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>In the bot rule menu, click <strong>📋 تکثیر قانون (Duplicate)</strong>.</li>
      <li>The system clones all filters, cleaners, headers, footers, and delay configurations into a fresh rule draft.</li>
      <li>Simply update the source and destination IDs to activate.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="origin-masking">Intermediate Channel Origin Masking</h2>
    <p>
      For enterprise operators wishing to hide the relationship between private internal research channels and public broadcasts, AutoTelegramForward supports an <em>intermediate staging channel</em> topology. Posts route from Source → Private Relay → Destination, stripping all internal metadata before final publication.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
